The costs and charges of seizure and sale shall also be payable from the proceeds of the
property seized and they shall be as follows:-
(1)  The costs of proceeding to the estate of the party in default, a charge not exceeding
eight per centum on the amount due;
(2)  The removal of the goods seized in case such removal takes place, a charge not
exceeding eight per centum on the amount due;
(3)  For keeping the same in safe custody in case of such removal, a charge not exceeding
one rupee per day;
(4)  For keeping a person in possession if the goods seized are not removed, a charge not
exceeding one rupee per day;
(5)  For  the expenses of  sale when any sale takes place, a charge not exceeding two and
half per centum on the nett proceeds of  the sale.
